Proposed (11.0s): Use when a picture of a UI must become real code, or when real code must be proven to match that picture. Trigger on any visual reference — a mockup, Figma export, whiteboard photo, competitor screenshot, codex render, or an already-built reference surface — that someone wants rebuilt as measured HTML/CSS against their design tokens, however rough or exact the ask sounds. Also trigger when a running implementation (dev server, Storybook, Tauri, localhost URL) is said to have drifted from a mockup or reference, when someone wants to know exactly what differs and by how many pixels, when they ask for diff rects or a gate against a design, or when they ask what the process is for getting a build pixel-identical to mockups. Covers one state or a batch of them. Claude measures on a ruler grid and directs, Codex writes markup, screenshot-and-diff rounds converge. Needs Codex CLI and npx Playwright.

